  "prefLabel": "Alc 102.02 Certified recovery support worker (CRSW)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Alc 102.02 “Certified recovery support worker (CRSW)” means “certified recovery support worker” as defined in RSA 330-C:2, IV, namely, “an individual certified by the office of professional licensure and certification to provide recovery support to persons with substance use disorders, who meets the qualifications in this chapter.”\n\nSource. #8169, eff 9-21-04; ss by 9417, eff 3-14-09; ss by #14585, eff 6-1-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/alc100-500.html"
